	As someone else has already mentioned, you can occasionally
find cans of grease laying about the dungeon.  I've never bothered to
identify one to find out if they have limited applications, but I've
yet to run out.  I would also guess that grease can eventually wear
off, but I haven't experienced it yet, so I can't say for sure.
Applying grease will only protect you against future corrosion; to
remove existing rust, you need to rustproof the item.  You can do that
by confusing yourself, then reading a (non-cursed) scroll of enchant
armor/weapon over it.  I have also heard this is good for fire-
proofing leather or wooden items, but I have yet to test that.

